---
source: system/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"swapoff\")"
---
Disable devices and files for paging and swapping.

Calls swapoff(2) to deactivate swap areas. The kernel pages all swap contents back to RAM before
deactivating, which may take significant time if the swap is heavily used.

Usage: swapoff [OPTIONS] [DEVICES]...

Arguments:
  [DEVICES]...
          Devices or files to disable

Options:
  -a, --all
          Disable all active swap areas

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
